/-!
# Every block of `hello1.w`'s x64 code at its place

Generated by `scc --arch x64 --code`. `hello1Asm` is the text `scc` wrote with
the length of each instruction and the offsets of its labels as GNU `as`
assembled it (untrusted: the canonical loader checks them, `SizeCheck`);
`hello1Cells` and `hello1Secs` are the code cells and the data sections the
canonical loader reads from it (`Scc.Sem.X64.cellsOf`,
`Scc.Sem.dataSections`, at elaboration time); the kernel cannot run the
parsers, so these two equations are the trust boundary, checked by
evaluation (`#guard`).

Per function, the table of its `block_spec` blocks (`scc --blocks`, named in
comments), grouped by the label before them with their instruction counts
and byte offsets from it, in program order; `hello1T_in` checks them all
against `hello1Cells` by `kernel_rfl` (`blocksIn`,
`Scc/Cert/Rt/CodeX64.lean`): every block is code at its label and offset in
every valid layout of the cells (`codeAt_of_blocksIn`), the loaded thread's
included (`lays_threadAt`, `endPc_threadAt`). `hello1_print`, `hello1_abort`
and `hello1_morestack` (with `hello1_mainTail` and `hello1_printL`, when
stated) check the code the runtime's proofs take as hypotheses (`Scc/Cert/Rt/X64Print.lean`, `X64Abort.lean`,
`X64MorestackIn.lean`).

`hello1Λ` is the layout of the program's static link (`Scc.Cert.Link`),
with the program's immediate table `hello1Imms` when stated (`Layout.imms`):
`hello1Λ_wf` its well-formedness, `hello1Λ_aborts` its abort labels in the
code, `hello1Λ_image` each data symbol's item in its image
(`Scc.Cert.Link.image_symbols`), `hello1Λ_load` the canonical loader's checks
of it (but the entry state's), with a valid layout of the loaded thread
(`validLayout_of_loadOk`). `hello1_wide`, if stated, puts the program in the
one-word fragment (`Scc.Cert.WideX64.wideIn`), so its certification
semantics writes words only (`wideSt_threadAt`). `hello1Need`, if stated, is
the stack need of its stack-checked functions, checked on `hello1Cells`
(`hello1Need_ok`, `Scc/Cert/NeedX64.lean`).
-/

